---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy";
const lastUpdated = "23 July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <div class="cnf-privacy">
      <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</em></p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data Club na Fealsúnachta
        ("we", "us") collects through clubnafealsunachta.com, why we
        collect it, and what rights you have over it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Club na Fealsúnachta is run by
        Francis Quinn, based in Trieste, Italy. For any
        question about this policy or your data, contact
        <a href="mailto:info@clubnafealsunachta.com">info@clubnafealsunachta.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Member account:</strong> if you join the club through the
          site, we store your username, email address, and a hashed
          (never plain-text) password.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form:</strong> if you message us, your name, email,
          and message are sent to our inbox by email. We do not store this
          in a database.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, your email address
          is sent to our mailing list provider, Mailchimp, who handles
          delivery and unsubscribes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Login session:</strong> when you log in, a strictly
          necessary session cookie is set in your browser so you stay
          signed in. It is not used for tracking or advertising.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        We use this data only to run the club: to create and secure your
        member account, to reply to messages sent through the contact
        form, and to send the newsletter to people who asked for it. We do
        not sell or share your data for advertising purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of external services to run the site, each
        of which processes data on our behalf:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts our database, including member
          accounts (data region: West EU (Ireland)).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mailchimp</strong> (United States) — manages newsletter
          delivery and subscriptions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google / Gmail</strong> (United States) — relays contact
          form messages to our inbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify</strong> (United States) — hosts the site and
          processes server logs, which include IP addresses, for every
          request.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Member accounts are kept until you ask us to delete them.
        Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Contact form
        and topic suggestion messages aren't stored in a database, but the
        email itself remains in our inbox until we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under GDPR, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or
        export your personal data, and to withdraw consent (e.g.
        unsubscribe from the newsletter) at any time. To exercise any of
        these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:info@clubnafealsunachta.com">info@clubnafealsunachta.com</a>
        and we'll handle your request directly — this isn't yet a
        self-service feature on the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data
        protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use one strictly necessary cookie to keep you logged in. We
        don't use analytics or advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site changes. The "last updated"
        date above will always reflect the latest version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
